  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 2.4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.4" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>And þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is þonne ærest<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.25"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he his agenne wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.26"/> Criste ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.27"/> þam cyningce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.28"/> gesylle, ⁊ mid þam hine sylfne inlagie to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.4" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>And þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is þonne ærost, þæt he his agenne wær Cryste ⁊ þam cyningce gesylle, ⁊ mid þam hyne sylfne inlagie to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>Et hoc tunc imprimis sit, ut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.11"/> weram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.1"/> suam (pretium natalis sui) Christo persoluat et regi, et per eam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.1"/> (hoc) se inlegiet ad emendandum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.4" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="281" ed="#liebermann"/>Que quidem primum est, ut sua redempcione se Deo et regi tradat; et inde se inleget ad emendacionem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.4" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="156" ed="#robertson"/>And þæt is þonne ærest, þæt he his agenne wer Criste ⁊ þam cyningce gesylle ⁊ mid þam hine sylfne inlagie to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="234" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And þæt is þonne ærest: þæt he his agenne wer Criste and þam cyningce gesylle, and mid þam hine sylfne inlagie to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="281" ed="#liebermann"/>und nämlich zuerst nun, dass er sein eigenes Wergeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#missing"/> der Kirche und dem König zahle und hiermit sich selbst in den Friedensgenuss einkaufe zur Bussfähigkeit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">and namely, first, that he pay his own wergild to Christ and to the king, and thereby buy himself back into the law so as to be allowed to make amends.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-4.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="157" ed="#robertson"/>And the first condition is, that he shall give his own wergeld to Christ and to the king and by that means obtain the legal right to offer compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="235" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And this is first: that he pay his own wergild to Christ and the king, and thereby make himself eligible to pay compensation.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="281"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_2">VIII Atr 2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="435"><label>same term (mægbot)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_74-2">Ine 74.2</ref> <quote>The compound mægbot occurs in i Cnut in respect to violating church peace, for which the offender has to pay his own wer (§2.4)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">In G, ‘⁊ þam’ was written twice but erased. 2.4 is missing from the Instituta Cnuti. Liebermann compares VIII Atr 2.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 281, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ærost <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ærost Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wær Cryste <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wær Cryste Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ þam <hi rend="italic">wiederholt, aber radirt G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ þam repeated, but erased G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ng gesille <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ng gesille Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ne <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> hoc <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ne Lond; hoc Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_2-4.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">280</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond; eingeklammertes übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">what precedes the bracket Lond; what is bracketed the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_2-4.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. with this clause and the one following, VIII Atr. 2; 3.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
